210-p53-joe-minetti-200m.jpg","c":"PHOTOS FROM THE CLUB CHAMPIONSHIPS\n\nJoe Minetti (33) completes a sprint double by winning the 200m from Stuart Paton who clocked a nippy 22.9 - not bad for a middle distance man! Others in shot , left to right, are Mike Scott, Andy Paton, Phil Smith and Pat Lyttle","id":"B210-42","w":"October 1986"},{"f":"crops/B218/B218-p06-andy-paton.jpg","c":"Andy Paton has been showing good form this winter, turning out in League cross-country races, road relays and road 10ks - he was 5th in the Surrey Championship 10k at Epsom.","id":"B218-19","w":"May 1992"},{"f":"crops/B218/B218-p36-paton-brothers-nower.jpg","c":"Below: The Brothers Paton, Stuart (71) and Andy (72) get well involved in the initial charge up the hill at The Nower, Dorking in Reebok Surrey League match 3.","id":"B218-79","w":"May 1992"},{"f":"crops/B218/B218-p38-montage-foote-ward-mazzotta-hobbs-paton-anderson.jpg","c":"Above: Top left to right - Ollie Foote, second Belgravian home at Coulsdon, a hirsute Frank Ward (we hear he has taken it off for his wedding) and Marco Mazzotta., who has steadily improved since last Autumn. Bottom - Jon Hobbs, Andy Paton and Don Anderson, the man who runs the Club '10' and then goes round again to collect the flags (and probably went round before to set them up!","id":"B218-79","w":"May 1992"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B208/B208-p30-paton-hollingworth.jpg","caption":"Right; Another Paton!!! Yes it's Andy sporting a healthy tan after 5 weeks holiday in Greece handing over to Dave Hollingworth who has gained many points for our Southern League team running as 'A' string steeplechaser.","source":"B208-69","when":"October 1984"},"slarchive":"https://slarchive.org/#athlete/andy-paton","slRaces":16,"x":1,"share":{"d":"Andy Paton in The Belgravian, the Belgrave Harriers club gazette, 1983–1993: 80 mentions in 15 issues, 56 race results and 5 photographs.","img":"https://belgravian-images.stephendgardner.workers.dev/belgravian/crops/B218/B218-p06-and